Recent advancements in light field imaging have enabled more accurate depth estimation, which has significant applications in 3D video processing, virtual reality, and augmented reality. However, traditional methods often struggle with occlusions due to the limitations of available data. To address this issue, we introduce a novel approach that incorporates occlusion-awareness into depth estimation. By leveraging occlusion-aware depth estimation, we can successfully recover hidden objects behind obstructions. To train this method, we introduce a new task called Occlusion-aware Expense Creator, which generates occlusion-aware depth maps from light field images. Our approach is versatile and can be applied to various depth estimation architectures, and we demonstrate its effectiveness on two prominent models, specifically a CNN-based method and a CNN-RNN method. Experiment results show that our approach significantly improves the performance of these models, especially in scenarios with occlusions. Furthermore, we also observe improvements in cases with motion and texture similarities. Our code will be publicly available upon publication. Keywords: Occlusion-aware Depth, Light Field Imaging, Depth Estimation, Occlusion-Aware Expense Creator. \end{abstract} 

